From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bastiaan van der Plaat <bastiaan.v.d.plaat@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 07:09:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add the DS system layer

sys_nds.c switches the ARM9 to 134 MHz in DSi mode and runs Quake in a
thread with a 64 KiB stack in main RAM, the ARM9 stack is in the 16 KiB
DTCM and Quake keeps arrays of up to 32 KiB on the stack. The hunk takes
all RAM that is left, 4 MiB on the DS and 16 MiB on the DSi. While Quake
starts the touch screen shows its title in Quake's brown, whether there
is an SD card, which game loads (the shareware, the full game, a mission
pack or a mod) and a dot for every few lines of the log like DOOM's, the
log goes to the
no$gba debug output, until the video driver takes the touch screen.
Errors are shown on the touch screen, the video driver stops changing
its palette and the power button still works there. Extra arguments
come from /data/quake/args.txt, a tick task keeps the tick counter
behind Sys_FloatTime running, which works it out in double precision.

The game data embedded in the ROM (nitro:/id1) is searched before the
same directory on the SD card, /data/quake/id1/, which gets the config
and savegames. Without an SD card everything comes from the ROM. The
player is named after the user of the DS settings.
---
 WinQuake/common.c  |  28 ++-
 WinQuake/sys.h     |   3 +
 WinQuake/sys_nds.c | 419 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 446 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 WinQuake/sys_nds.c

diff --git a/WinQuake/common.c b/WinQuake/common.c
index 38f631c..c9925a6 100644
--- a/WinQuake/common.c
+++ b/WinQuake/common.c
@@ -1728,6 +1728,26 @@ void COM_AddGameDirectory (char *dir)
 
 }
 
+/*
+================
+COM_AddBaseGameDirectory
+
+Adds basedir/game, on the Nintendo DS the game data embedded in the ROM
+comes first so the SD card can add to it and gets the written files
+================
+*/
+static void COM_AddBaseGameDirectory (char *basedir, char *game)
+{
+	char	romdir[MAX_OSPATH];
+
+	sprintf (romdir, "nitro:/%s", game);
+	COM_AddGameDirectory (romdir);
+	if (!strcmp (basedir, "nitro:"))
+		return;
+	Sys_mkdir (va("%s/%s", basedir, game));
+	COM_AddGameDirectory (va("%s/%s", basedir, game));
+}
+
 /*
 ================
 COM_InitFilesystem
@@ -1778,12 +1798,12 @@ void COM_InitFilesystem (void)
 //
 // start up with GAMENAME by default (id1)
 //
-	COM_AddGameDirectory (va("%s/"GAMENAME, basedir) );
+	COM_AddBaseGameDirectory (basedir, GAMENAME);
 
 	if (COM_CheckParm ("-rogue"))
-		COM_AddGameDirectory (va("%s/rogue", basedir) );
+		COM_AddBaseGameDirectory (basedir, "rogue");
 	if (COM_CheckParm ("-hipnotic"))
-		COM_AddGameDirectory (va("%s/hipnotic", basedir) );
+		COM_AddBaseGameDirectory (basedir, "hipnotic");
 
 //
 // -game <gamedir>
@@ -1793,7 +1813,7 @@ void COM_InitFilesystem (void)
 	if (i && i < com_argc-1)
 	{
 		com_modified = true;
-		COM_AddGameDirectory (va("%s/%s", basedir, com_argv[i+1]));
+		COM_AddBaseGameDirectory (basedir, com_argv[i+1]);
 	}
 
 //
